From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Atharva Tyagi <tyagiatharva11@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 21:56:07 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] lsf_horMnSubTerms=1 crashes with moisture off: guard two
 unallocated pointers

Running a DRY LES with subsidence on -- lsfSelector=1 and lsf_horMnSubTerms=1,
moistureSelector=0 -- dies on the first timestep with

    GPUassert: an illegal memory access was encountered
               ../TIME_INTEGRATION/CUDA/cuda_timeIntDevice.cu 135

Two unguarded moisture accesses, both in the subsidence path:

1. cuda_lsfSlabMeans() launches the qv slab-mean kernel unconditionally
   (over &moistScalars_d[0]), but cuda_moistureDeviceSetup() only allocates
   moistScalars_d inside `if (moistureSelector > 0)` (cuda_moistureDevice.cu:41).
   With moisture off that pointer is an unassigned global, so the launch reads
   through null on the device.

2. cudaDevice_lsfRHS writes Frhs_qv[ijk] unconditionally inside the
   `lsf_horMnSubTerms_d == 1` branch. Frhs_qv points into moistScalarsFrhs_d,
   allocated under the same guard, so it is the same bug on the write side.

Both are now guarded by moistureSelector / moistureSelector_d. lsf_numPhiVars
stays 5 and the qv profile slot stays zeroed by the existing memset, so the
rho/u/v/theta subsidence terms are bit-for-bit unchanged and a moist run is
unaffected.

Same class as the NORHO bug in 692a3cd: a pointer used outside the condition
that allocates it. The consequence differs only in luck -- that one found zeroed
heap and produced inf, this one finds null and traps.

Verified: 400 steps and 20,000 steps dry with subsidence on now complete with no
CORRUPTED report, all fields finite, k0/k1 = 0.807.
---
 .../CUDA/cuda_largeScaleForcingsDevice.cu     | 30 ++++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/SRC/HYDRO_CORE/CUDA/cuda_largeScaleForcingsDevice.cu b/SRC/HYDRO_CORE/CUDA/cuda_largeScaleForcingsDevice.cu
index c0eb479..b64a34d 100644
--- a/SRC/HYDRO_CORE/CUDA/cuda_largeScaleForcingsDevice.cu
+++ b/SRC/HYDRO_CORE/CUDA/cuda_largeScaleForcingsDevice.cu
@@ -123,11 +123,21 @@ extern "C" int cuda_lsfSlabMeans(){
                                                               &lsf_slabMeanPhiProfiles_d[iFldProf*fldProfStride]);
    }//end for iFldProf
    //Blank out the temporary storage and atmonic result
-   iFldProf=lsf_numPhiVars-1; //qv
-   iFld=0;
-   cuda_singleRankHorizSlabMeans<<<grid_red, tBlock_red>>>(&hydroFlds_d[RHO_INDX*fldStride],
-                                                           &moistScalars_d[iFld*fldStride],lsf_meanPhiBlock_d,
-                                                           &lsf_slabMeanPhiProfiles_d[iFldProf*fldProfStride]);
+   /* KEGONSA FIX: this qv slab-mean was UNGUARDED upstream, and moistScalars_d is only
+    * allocated when moistureSelector > 0 (cuda_moistureDevice.cu:41). Running dry with
+    * lsf_horMnSubTerms = 1 therefore launched a kernel over a null device pointer and
+    * died with "an illegal memory access was encountered" at the first timestep. The
+    * profile slot stays zeroed by the memset above, and the matching read in
+    * cudaDevice_lsfRHS is guarded the same way, so subsidence on rho/u/v/theta is
+    * unaffected. Same class of bug as the NORHO one (fork commit 692a3cd): a pointer
+    * used outside the condition that allocates it. */
+   if(moistureSelector > 0){
+     iFldProf=lsf_numPhiVars-1; //qv
+     iFld=0;
+     cuda_singleRankHorizSlabMeans<<<grid_red, tBlock_red>>>(&hydroFlds_d[RHO_INDX*fldStride],
+                                                             &moistScalars_d[iFld*fldStride],lsf_meanPhiBlock_d,
+                                                             &lsf_slabMeanPhiProfiles_d[iFldProf*fldProfStride]);
+   }
 #ifdef DEBUG
    if(mpi_rank_world==0){
      printf("lsf_horMnSubTerms for phi-fields complete.\n");
@@ -244,9 +254,13 @@ __device__ void cudaDevice_lsfRHS(float temp_freq_fac, float* rho,
                                                -lsf_slabMeanPhiProfiles_d[3*fldProfStride+k-1]/lsf_slabMeanPhiProfiles_d[0*fldProfStride+k-1])
                                               /(zPos_d[ijkp1]-zPos_d[ijkm1]);
       /*qv*/
-      Frhs_qv[ijk] = Frhs_qv[ijk]-f_lsf_w*rho[ijk]*(lsf_slabMeanPhiProfiles_d[4*fldProfStride+k+1]/lsf_slabMeanPhiProfiles_d[0*fldProfStride+k+1]
-                                          -lsf_slabMeanPhiProfiles_d[4*fldProfStride+k-1]/lsf_slabMeanPhiProfiles_d[0*fldProfStride+k-1])
-                                         /(zPos_d[ijkp1]-zPos_d[ijkm1]);
+      /* KEGONSA FIX: guarded, for the same reason as the slab-mean launch above --
+       * Frhs_qv points into moistScalarsFrhs_d, which is unallocated when running dry. */
+      if(moistureSelector_d > 0){
+        Frhs_qv[ijk] = Frhs_qv[ijk]-f_lsf_w*rho[ijk]*(lsf_slabMeanPhiProfiles_d[4*fldProfStride+k+1]/lsf_slabMeanPhiProfiles_d[0*fldProfStride+k+1]
+                                            -lsf_slabMeanPhiProfiles_d[4*fldProfStride+k-1]/lsf_slabMeanPhiProfiles_d[0*fldProfStride+k-1])
+                                           /(zPos_d[ijkp1]-zPos_d[ijkm1]);
+      }
     }
 
   }
